From 87fd33c5b494d151ccb5cad630b364b09e961c9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:10:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the VRR row of the player information on one line,
 and Kodi's word for Off in the Spanish help
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The value of the VRR row while the refresh follows the video ("On at the output: the refresh follows
the video", and in Spanish "Activado en la salida: el refresco sigue al vídeo") took two lines of the
second column of the System page since the change that measures the signal by the out-fences, and that
column then took 565 of its 564 px with every row shown: its last row was cut (skin_check.py of
tools/regress/playerinfo). It now says, on one line in the four languages,
that the refresh follows the video and that the TV or monitor may say another rate in its own
information (the rate of the mode): "Follows the video; TV may say other Hz", "Sigue al vídeo; la tele
dirá otros Hz". The help of the setting says it in full.

The Spanish help of "Video at its own rate with VRR" names the value "Off" as Kodi's own translations
of #351 show it in es_es, es_ar and es_mx: "Apagado" (resource.language.es_* of Piers).

Checked: tools/regress/playerinfo (skin_check.py: the column takes 531 of its 564 px; every label fits
in the four languages; po_check.py).
---
 .../language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po           | 4 ++--
 .../language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po           | 8 ++++----
 .../language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po           | 8 ++++----
 .../language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po           | 8 ++++----
 4 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

